  "notes": "⚠ **A deliberately windowed entry, and the window is the model.** `rnb-2000s` holds his 2005–2010 entry and flags that \"his 2011+ material sits closer to the trap-soul lane\"; this covers **2011–2019 only** and does not restate that era. The defining change is harmonic and the entry says so: \"the 2011+ material moves to minor-mode 2-chord loops with m9 pads, abandoning the jazz-piano chord beds of his earlier era. That harmonic simplification is the window's defining change\" — so `maxChords` is 2 and the families are the loop pair. ⚠ **`session.keys` is left inherited on purpose.** The entry names exactly one centre, \"B major recurs across his catalogue\", and no shipped model in this dataset authors a single key; the parent's five-key list already carries B minor, and `scales` is authored with `major` so the documented colour survives. That is a deliberate omission rather than an oversight. The kit is stated in full — \"808 kick on 1 and the 16th before 3, hard clap on beat 3, offbeat 808 maraca, dense swung 16th hats with triplet conga fills and 32nd rolls\" — so a shaker and a conga sit on the offbeat and the roll vocabulary carries both subdivisions; \"the up-tempo club cuts flatten to 2&4 with continuous 16th hats\" is `fullTimeVariantProb`. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are the swing amount, every drum number and the 808 slide figures. ⚠ `confidence` is medium, mirroring the entry. ⚠ `session.bpm.mode` is **INFERRED**: the number is not stated in the entry, and it is an authored centre of gravity inside the band the entry does state. ⚠ **The id carries the window, not the name.** The unqualified `trey-songz` id belongs to the primary 2005–2010 entry that `rnb-2000s` holds; this file is only the windowed half, so it takes the qualified id and leaves the canonical one free — the same convention `carvin-and-ivan-neo-soul-half` already uses for the volume's other split of this kind.",
